WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.360
A color-mounted sensor now records the exact particle level's wildlife breath during wildfire smoke events. This is Planetterrian Daily, episode 207. Jonathan The Tortoise carries 287 unique gene variants and maintains low methylation entropy. A science advances paper links these features to exceptional longevity in the oldest known land vertebrate. Researchers examined methylation patterns across the lifespan. The animal is

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:36.820
194 years old. Colorado State University researchers develop an open-source smoke logger that attaches

00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:42.580
to animal collars and records hazardous particle concentrations. The device pairs with existing

00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:48.680
wildlife tracking systems for location and physiological data. Initial results appear in methods

00:00:48.680 --> 00:00:54.540
in ecology and evolution. Professor George Wittemeyer led the project with US Forest Service

00:00:54.540 --> 00:01:01.520
ecologist Mark Dittmer and postdoctoral researcher Adam Parlin. The logger addresses the absence of

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:06.520
air quality monitoring in remote wilderness areas where smoke plumes now persist for weeks.

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:12.160
Researchers designed the unit to be small, affordable, and freely available for other field

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:17.400
teams. The collar-mounted smoke logger gives researchers the first direct view of particle

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:23.360
concentrations animals experience during prolonged wildfire events. Previous studies relied on

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:28.860
distant ground stations or satellite estimates that missed fine-scale exposure. By pairing

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:34.360
the logger with GPS and heart rate collars, teams can now match specific smoke levels to

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:40.200
changes in movement, foraging, or stress markers. The open source design means any wildlife

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:45.760
group can build and deploy units without new hardware purchases. Most people assume bacteria

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:52.260
simply grab whatever iron they find and keep growing. In reality, pseudomonas aruginosa runs a

00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:58.200
two protein switch that checks iron both outside and inside the cell before rewriting large

00:01:58.200 --> 00:01:59.920
sections of its own metabolism.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:05.360
The system lets the pathogen adjust energy production and virulence factors to match the

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.860
iron poor environment inside a human host.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:13.860
Once the switch flips, the bacterium rewrites large portions of its metabolic network in

00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.360
a single coordinated response.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:21.680
This matters for anyone who has taken antibiotics because iron availability inside tissues can

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.460
change how effectively the drug clears the infection.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:29.640
The next result that would settle remaining questions is a direct test of whether blocking

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:34.960
the two protein sensor reduces bacterial survival in animal models of lung infection.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:41.040
A new nature study maps regulatory cells that control immune activity before tumors form.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:45.860
The framework targets these cells to prevent progression in at-risk lung tissue.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:49.560
Researchers describe it as a root to earlier intervention.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.940
The work focuses on one lung cancer subtype.

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:58.340
Stanford researchers designed a molecule that redirects a lymphoma-promoting protein to

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.960
activate cancer cell self-destruction pathways.

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:06.140
In mice, the treatment cleared aggressive human lymphoma tumors within 11 days.

00:03:06.800 --> 00:03:09.940
The approach differs from simple blockade of tumor growth.

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:12.640
Testing remains at the preclinical stage.

00:03:13.280 --> 00:03:18.980
Scientists found that vitamin D2 intake reduces the body's vitamin D3, the form produced

00:03:18.980 --> 00:03:20.220
by sunlight exposure.

00:03:20.940 --> 00:03:26.000
Prior work indicates vitamin D3 supplies stronger protection against viruses and bacteria.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:29.820
The study compared supplement forms directly in participants.

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:34.460
The finding applies to people who rely on supplements for vitamin D status.

00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:40.840
An analysis of 22 studies examined trans fats naturally present in milk, butter, yogurt

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:41.480
and cheese.

00:03:42.140 --> 00:03:46.800
These dairy trans fats produce no increase in heart disease, stroke, cardiovascular

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.720
ofascular death or type 2 diabetes risk.

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:53.540
Control trials found no adverse changes in blood lipids.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:56.220
Long-term observational data confirmed

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.300
the absence of elevated disease rates.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:01.600
The results contrast with industrial trans fats

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:03.480
from partially hydrogenated oils.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:08.000
Researchers examined more than 130,000 births in Georgia.

00:04:08.660 --> 00:04:10.740
Hundreds of fathers died within five years

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:11.820
of the child's arrival.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:14.880
Roughly 60% of those deaths were classified

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:21.880
as potentially preventable. Homicide, accidental injury, suicide, and drug overdose accounted for

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:28.040
most preventable cases. The study identifies a gap in public health tracking of paternal mortality.

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:34.120
Photosynthetic organisms in the Baltic Sea form colonies that increase sinking rates of biomass.

00:04:34.920 --> 00:04:40.360
The process transports carbon from surface waters to deeper layers. Stockholm University

00:04:40.360 --> 00:04:44.900
researchers quantified the contribution of colonial versus single-cell forms.

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:49.280
Aggregation behavior determines how much carbon reaches the seafloor.

00:04:49.900 --> 00:04:55.140
Mary Brenda Acoda developed the Seymour algorithm that reconstructs images in one step.

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:59.620
The system maintains diagnostic quality while a cutting acquisition time.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:05.300
NLNG presented the tool to Nigerian health stakeholders for clinical rollout.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.040
No new hardware is required for deployment.

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:13.740
A frontiers and organizational psychology study found women perceive errors more harshly

00:05:13.740 --> 00:05:15.320
when male colleagues are present.

00:05:15.820 --> 00:05:19.400
The effect did not appear when women worked primarily with other women.

00:05:20.200 --> 00:05:22.980
Researchers collected data across office environments.

00:05:23.600 --> 00:05:27.660
The pattern points to social context as a modulator of error appraisal.

00:05:28.380 --> 00:05:33.320
Large language models recommended status quo policies twice as often as new approaches

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:34.860
when asked for climate advice.

00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:38.320
The study reviewed multiple models and prompt types.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:41.780
The bias toward familiar options emerged consistently.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:45.360
Researchers linked the pattern to training data distributions.

00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:50.920
Microphones placed on soybean plants captured sounds from hidden insects in the field.

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:55.060
Emily Sir's work combines entomology with acoustic monitoring.

00:05:55.760 --> 00:05:59.640
The approach aims to flag pest presence before visible damage occurs.

00:06:00.340 --> 00:06:03.140
Recordings were taken directly in muddy field conditions.

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:09.740
higher prices on candy, soft drinks, and beer prompted fewer border crossings than prior models predicted.

00:06:10.660 --> 00:06:16.520
Danish data showed limited leakage despite tax differences. The study revised earlier assumptions

00:06:16.520 --> 00:06:23.520
about consumer response. Revenue impacts remained smaller than forecasted. Nearly 1,000 papers mapped

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:29.680
connections among technology, investor psychology, and market risk. The analysis identified three

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:35.560
separate conceptual bases rather than one unified framework. Psychological factors and algorithm

00:06:35.560 --> 00:06:41.400
design emerged as separate pillars. The mapping covers automated investment guidance and decision

00:06:41.400 --> 00:06:47.460
biases. Before we go, researchers plan a direct test of whether blocking the two protein iron

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:53.640
sensor reduces bacterial survival in animal models of lung infection. That covers today's science

